  "flavor_text": {
    "one_line": "A mountain caste culture of pass-forts, mine law, and ancestral accounting.",
    "one_paragraph": "The Vaskari build upward and inward, raising stark stone citadels over switchback roads while carving vaults for ledgers, dead, and armories beneath them. They respect rank earned through labor, command, and proven endurance, but even high houses are constrained by old tunnel law and collective mine shares. Outsiders are tolerated when useful, never trusted with the deep roads, and judged by whether their word weighs as much as iron."
